{% extends "layouts/docs" %}

{% block content %}
<p>A Kiln template is ordinary text, usually HTML, with three kinds of delimiters mixed in. Everything outside them is output as written.</p>

<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>&#123;{ expression }}</code></td><td>Output the value of an expression</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>&#123;% tag %}</code></td><td>Run a tag, such as <code>if</code> or <code>for</code></td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>&#123;# comment #}</code></td><td>A comment. It produces no output</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>

{% apply example(context: { user: { name: "Ada" }, messages: 3 }) %}
{% verbatim %}
{# Greets the signed-in user #}
{% if user %}
<p>Hello, {{ user.name }}. You have {{ messages }} messages.</p>
{% endif %}
{% endverbatim %}
{% endapply %}

<p>Comments can span several lines, but they don't nest.</p>

<h2>Whitespace</h2>

<p>Kiln removes any line that holds only tags or comments, including its line break. Indent your tags to match your HTML, and the output still comes out clean.</p>

{% apply example(context: { items: ["Tea", "Coffee"] }) %}
{% verbatim %}
<ul>
	{% for item in items %}
	<li>{{ item }}</li>
	{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endverbatim %}
{% endapply %}

<p>Output tags never remove their line, because they print something.</p>

<p>To remove whitespace by hand, add a <code>-</code> inside a delimiter. It removes all whitespace on that side, including line breaks.</p>

{% apply example(context: { label: "Save" }) %}
{% verbatim %}
<button>
	{{- label -}}
</button>
{% endverbatim %}
{% endapply %}

<p>Every delimiter supports it: <code>&#123;{-</code>, <code>-}}</code>, <code>&#123;%-</code>, <code>-%}</code>, <code>&#123;#-</code> and <code>-#}</code>.</p>

<h2>Strings</h2>

<p>Strings use single or double quotes. Double-quoted strings can include expressions with <code>#{ }</code>:</p>

{% apply example(context: { user: { name: "ada" }, count: 2 }) %}
{% verbatim %}
{{ "Hello #{ user.name|title }, you have #{ count } new messages" }}
{% endverbatim %}
{% endapply %}

<p>Both quote styles support the escapes <code>\\</code>, <code>\'</code>, <code>\"</code>, <code>\n</code>, <code>\r</code>, <code>\t</code> and <code>\u{hex}</code>. Write <code>\#{</code> for a literal <code>#{</code>.</p>

<h2>Names</h2>

<p>Variable, function and filter names start with a letter or underscore, followed by letters, digits or underscores. They are case-sensitive. Kiln's own names use camelCase, such as <code>formatDate</code> and <code>loop.revIndex</code>.</p>

<p>These words are reserved and can't be variable names: <code>true</code>, <code>false</code>, <code>null</code>, <code>and</code>, <code>or</code>, <code>not</code>, <code>in</code>, <code>is</code>, <code>loop</code> and <code>slots</code>.</p>

<h2>Template names</h2>

<p>Templates are named by their path, such as <code>pages/home.kiln</code> or <code>components/card</code>.</p>

<ul>
	<li>The <code>.kiln</code> extension is optional.</li>
	<li>Names starting with <code>./</code> or <code>../</code> are relative to the current template.</li>
	<li>Other names are relative to the loader's root folder.</li>
	<li>A name can't point above the root folder.</li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}
